You know, everyone complains about the
wand-of-death-wielding-dwarf-at-the-top-of-the-Mines-or-worse-yet-on-Dungeon-level-one.
My experience is, that sort of thing happens very, very rarely. It
seems to me that they're generated much farther down in the dungeon.
I'm not sure I've ever encountered a monster wielding the dreaded WoD
before I had reflection or MR.

>
>With Healers the "protection racket" actually makes some sense. Blitz for
>Minetown while still XL1 (let the pet do the work) and donate for
>intrinsic AC, then try and get out alive. After that I'd do Sokoban.

You know, I've tried that (not because I believe in it, but just to
see how well it would work). It so rarely works out to be worth it.
Even if you get down to Minetown alive, what you're left with is a
character who still doesn't have great AC (because he probably hasn't
picked up a lot of decent armor yet) and who can get killed with one
swipe. Several times I've been killed soon *after* donating to the
priest, because my pet died, or I fell through a trap, or for whatever
other reason couldn't get back up to relative safety to begin
levelling up.

(BTW, I know that you're against that strategy in general as well, and
I agree that if it makes sense for any character, it would be a
gnomish healer.)
