I'll second that advice, and mention that XP can be obtained without
levelling up, as well. 
>
>>Question #2:  at what point do you decide:  ok, I'm powerful enough to 
>>go on my quest?
>
>Depends on the Quest Nemesis. You can't do it until XL14; if your Nemesis
>is a pushover (like Valks), you want to do it right away. If your Nemesis
>requires special preparation, like the Cyclops (ie, the Healer Nemesis),
>you obviously will want to wait until you are ready. If your Nemesis is a
>hideous death machine, like Master Kaen (Monk), you may want to do it very
>late, perhaps after cleaning out the Castle and using the wishes.

When I went on my one Monk quest, I was convinced that I had to have a
WoD and zap him before he grabbed the Eyes, or all was lost. My wish
for it didn't work (must've mistyped; got a WoSleep instead). I ended
up deciding to go in anyway, and was surprised to find that, when I
got to Master Kaen's level, a) I couldn't see him (level was dark; did
see by telepathy, though), and b) my WoSleep shot merely missed and
woke him up. I just backed up to the upstairs and duked it out (I
wasn't going weaponless--had one of the Brands, I think), and Kaen was
gone pretty quick. I had a lot more trouble against the Chromatic
Dragon as a Caveman. It summoned a lot of nasties that very nearly
killed me after I had slain the Dragon (they swarmed before I could
grab the Bell or the Quest Artifact, so I couldn't just leave; they
were on top of the upstairs as well).

Anyway, I agree that for Valks, the Nemesis is so weak and the
Artifact is so incredibly useful that doing the quest ASAP makes a lot
of sense. I usually do the quest as soon as I level up to 14, but in
the process, I'm thinking it almost always makes sense to do the
Castle first--especially since I don't really want to thoroughly spoil
myself about each individual Quest Nemesis before going in.
